# Publishing source history

Use genuine publication and update dates, and write each change note for what affects a reader. This page owns the pinned sources and the record of how the upstream published-dates component moved into metadata. Other publishing pages link here instead of repeating it.

## Local documentation rule

Civica documentation front matter uses `published_on`, `updated_on` and `updates`. These are Civica authoring fields, not aliases accepted by the upstream Ruby gem.

Render update history as a native disclosure with semantic dates and readable notes. Keep it usable without JavaScript and do not open a long history automatically on page load. Do not invent a first-publication date for an older page. Recover it from the repository history or state the evidence limit. Do not attach a government organisation, official logo or GOV.UK analytics to local metadata.

Some official template guidance still lists the older published-dates component. Where its component table conflicts with the pinned implementation, use the migration record below and explain the difference. Do not reproduce a removed component.

## Reviewed source snapshot

The Publishing Design Guide extends the GOV.UK Design System and does not replace it. Its [About page](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/about/) separates guidance for the publishing platform from the core system. The component gem is a separate implementation library. Keep the three sources distinct when mapping a pattern to Home Assistant.

The inventory was reviewed on **11 November 2026** by following the three official section indexes and all nested guidance links. It records 42 canonical pages and a SHA-256 digest of each fetched HTML response. Trailing-slash aliases are counted once. The machine-readable record is `docs/data/publishing-inventory.json`.

The reviewed component source is [commit bbe236c](https://github.com/alphagov/govuk_publishing_components/tree/bbe236c5259dd84ddb9208cabca0186fd04d5faa). Its changelog’s latest numbered release is 71.1.0, with unreleased changes above it. The guide repository’s observed head is [f227dc0](https://github.com/alphagov/govuk-design-guide/commit/f227dc04ff5c25d91b81420f8db326e75757eceb). That records the repository observation. It is not an independently verified deployed build identifier.

## Published dates moved into metadata

The migration is verified. [Issue 5560](https://github.com/alphagov/govuk_publishing_components/issues/5560) proposed combining the two components. [Pull request 5572](https://github.com/alphagov/govuk_publishing_components/pull/5572) merged on **14 July 2026** and appears under version **66.9.0** in the [pinned changelog](https://github.com/alphagov/govuk_publishing_components/blob/bbe236c5259dd84ddb9208cabca0186fd04d5faa/CHANGELOG.md). It kept the old component at first to avoid a breaking change.

The old `published_dates` component was removed in **71.0.0**, through [pull request 5807](https://github.com/alphagov/govuk_publishing_components/pull/5807). The `see_updates_link` option was restored in **71.1.0**, through [pull request 5844](https://github.com/alphagov/govuk_publishing_components/pull/5844).

| Earlier published-dates input | Current metadata input | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `published` | `first_published` | First publication label |
| `history` array | `page_history` | Dated change entries |
| — | `last_updated` | Latest publication update label |
| — | `see_updates_link` | Link to the page-history disclosure |

Current `page_history` entries have `display_time`, `timestamp` and `note`. The metadata component also keeps a separate `history` text field. Do not confuse it with the old published-dates array. No current `show_history` option was found in the reviewed [implementation](https://github.com/alphagov/govuk_publishing_components/blob/bbe236c5259dd84ddb9208cabca0186fd04d5faa/app/views/govuk_publishing_components/components/_metadata.html.erb) or [examples](https://github.com/alphagov/govuk_publishing_components/blob/bbe236c5259dd84ddb9208cabca0186fd04d5faa/app/views/govuk_publishing_components/components/docs/metadata.yml).

